# Frozen terrain fill-face list - the reviewed LP faces that may back-fill
# sightlines no authored HP covers (water planes, level-boundary channels).
# One row per FILL face; the columns are
#     FILL <level> <sector> <face> <need-px> <provenance>
# and need-px/provenance record how the face earned its place.
#
# MEMBERSHIP IS THE VERDICT. The runtime consults a static list generated from
# this file (scripts/gen-fill-tags.py -> terrain_fill_tags.h), so a face that is
# absent simply does not fill - there is nothing for a rejected row to guard
# against, and the rejected-candidate rows the threshold classifiers needed are
# gone. Every candidate the sweep raises still has to be reviewed before it is
# written here; that review just leaves no residue when the answer is no.
#
# Two sanctioned ways to reach this file, both ending in a reviewed verdict:
#   1. the coverage sweep (scripts/terrain-fill-sweep.sh) + a per-face strip
#      review - the origin of every measured need-px row below;
#   2. the in-game inspector (P key):
#      aim at a face, read its identity and whether authored HP covers that
#      sightline, flip the verdict live, then fold the session file in with
#      scripts/fill-tags-apply.py. Rows it adds carry provenance `pick` and
#      need-px 0 - judged against the live scene, not a pixel measurement.
# NEVER hand-edit a row in without one of those.
